x669 puts x667 x668
x670 call close x669 
x671 call open x670 2
x672 write x671 2
x673 text "There are no loops in the body of a function. Repetition is fold and loop over an earlier function: the step function receives the state, the index, and any extra arguments, and returns the next state. loop adds a predicate function that is checked before each iteration. n may be a literal or a value. A literal count is bounded statically, against the per-function budget. A variable count is bounded by fuel in the reference interpreter; compiled targets have no execution budget, so it runs as many iterations as the value says."
x674 puts x672 x673
x675 call close x674 
