x753 call close x752 
x754 write x753 2
x755 text "e0 fn clamp u32 u32 u32 -> u32\nlo lt p0 p1\nhi lt p2 p0\na select lo p1 p0\nr select hi p2 a\nret r\n\n"
x756 puts x754 x755
x757 call open x756 6
x758 write x757 4
x759 write x758 2
x760 text "cm"
x761 puts x759 x760
x762 write x761 2
x763 text "# reply\n"
x764 puts x762 x763
x765 call close x764 
x766 write x765 2
x767 text "e0\nhi lt p2 a\nr select hi p2 a"
x768 puts x766 x767
x769 call close x768 
x770 call close x769 
x771 call close x770 
x772 call open x771 13
x773 write x772 4
x774 write x773 1
x775 text "diagnostics"
x776 puts x774 x775
x777 call open x776 11
x778 write x777 2
x779 text "Diagnostics"
x780 puts x778 x779
x781 call close x780 
x782 call open x781 2
x783 write x782 2
x784 text "Every rejection carries a stable code (parse, type, structure, handle, revision, limit), what was expected, what was seen, and the one fix that resolves it. The compiler never guesses: a reply that is ambiguous is rejected with the fix, not applied approximately."
x785 puts x783 x784
x786 call close x785 
x787 call close x786 
ret x787
end

